{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"7bef5355acf32b16","name":"card_event_shadow_strike","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/BloodIron/events/card_event_shadow_strike","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SHADOW STRIKE","text":"Give a friendly unit Shock. At the end of turn, give it Smokescreen if possible.","flavorText":"Early in WWII, fighter aircraft were largely ineffective at night due to limited visibility, and pilots were not trained for night landings. This allowed Japanese bombers to operate freely, although nighttime navigation was difficult, and bombs were rarely accurate. However, Japanese G4M \"Betty\" bomber pilots developed deadly night torpedo tactics, using bright floating flares to illuminate Allied ships, like at the Battle of Rennell Island in 1943. As the war progressed the Allies more or less managed to counter these attacks with the advancement of airborne radar technology which allowed night fighters to operate independently to locate and attack the Japanese bombers.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_shadow_strike","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_shadow_strike_title","SourceString":"SHADOW STRIKE","LocalizedString":"SHADOW STRIKE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_shadow_strike_text","SourceString":"Give a friendly unit Shock. At the end of turn, give it Smokescreen if possible.","LocalizedString":"Give a friendly unit Shock. At the end of turn, give it Smokescreen if possible."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_shadow_strike_history","SourceString":"Early in WWII, fighter aircraft were largely ineffective at night due to limited visibility, and pilots were not trained for night landings. This allowed Japanese bombers to operate freely, although nighttime navigation 